{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>That YHWH was with him.</b> It would have been fitting to say 'that Elohim was with him,' but Joseph's master was an Egyptian who did not know YHWH, and therefore it says that when he saw his great success, he supposed it was by way of the wisdom of sorcery, like the practices of the land of Egypt with which they are accustomed, until he saw that it was from the Most High, by means of a vision that appeared to him in a dream or in a pillar of cloud, for Joseph's honor. And this is what they said in the Midrash: וירא אדניו כי ה׳ אתו — he would see him whispering and entering while whispering and exiting. He would say 'mix boiling' and they would boil; 'mix lukewarm' and they would be lukewarm. And what did he say? יוסף תבן בעפריות, חרשין במצרים. Until when? Until he saw the Shekhinah standing upon him — as it is written, וירא אדניו כי ה׳ אתו."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:45.593700310Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}